WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.520
Glad to have you with us on Tesla's short time, Daily, Episode 475.

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:06.400
I'm Patrick and Vancouver.

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:09.380
Today is May 17th, 2026.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:11.880
Here's what you need to know about Tesla today.

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:18.960
Looking back at six episodes from 2026, May 11th to 2026, May 17th,

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:22.280
the stories that mattered, what we learned, and what to watch next.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:26.560
A Tesla completed the cross-country trip from New York to Los Angeles

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:29.540
on FSD supervises with zero interventions.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:33.640
The drive demonstrates the system's ability to handle varied highway

00:00:33.640 --> 00:00:35.980
and urban conditions over thousands of miles.

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:40.920
It provides fresh, real-world data that can refine future versions of the software.

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:45.960
This run shows how the current supervised system already covers long distances

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:47.140
and mixed environments.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.540
While the software keeps proving itself on the road,

00:00:51.020 --> 00:00:55.400
Tesla is also clearing physical production capacity for the next generation of vehicles.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:59.320
Production of both models has ended at the free-mod factory

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:03.500
after 14 years for the Model S and 11 years for the Model X.

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:07.400
The move clears assembly capacity that can now be redirected

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.320
toward current high-demand vehicles.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:14.940
It also marks the close of an era for Tesla's original flagship sedans and SUVs.

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:18.060
The final car is rolled off the line in recent days.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:22.540
With older platforms winding down, attention turns to how Tesla is

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:24.820
funding and expanding its newer factories.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:31.640
The Berlin plant received another $250 million in funding tied to its fast hiring push.

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:37.580
The capital supports ongoing expansion even as Tesla's broader robotics and AI plans

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:39.660
continue to draw from vehicle profits.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:45.580
This keeps the German site central to scaling both current production and future hardware ambitions.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:50.580
The additional money arrived after a period of rapid recruitment at the facility.

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:57.200
As Tesla invests in its own factories, competitors are also moving into the same energy storage space.

00:01:57.880 --> 00:02:03.160
Ford Energy introduced an LFP-powered DC block designed for 20 years of service

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:05.640
and over five megawatt hours of capacity.

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:10.540
The product directly competes with Tesla's Megapack in stationary storage.

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:16.340
It gives utilities and developers another option for grid-scale projects where longevity and

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:21.720
energy density matter. The new container targets the same utility and commercial customers

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:26.960
that have ordered Megapacks in the past. While rivals target Tesla's energy products,

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:32.000
Tesla itself is quietly improving how drivers interact with its charging network.

00:02:32.620 --> 00:02:38.520
A pilot system at five California and New York stations now places drivers on an automatic waitlist

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:41.880
with estimated times instead of requiring them to circle.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:48.340
The change reduces uncertainty at busy locations and gives Tesla data on real-time demand patterns.

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:51.240
Further roll-out details are still pending.

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:56.100
The feature went live at a handful of high traffic supercharger sites first.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:02.060
Better charging logistics matter most in markets where Tesla is still building its physical presence.

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:07.740
The Bangalore Center marks Tesla's latest step in building a physical presence in India

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:12.460
after years of import-only sales. Staff will handle demonstrations,

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:16.040
test drives, and order support for the model-wide lineup.

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:21.460
Success here would validate Tesla's approach of entering markets with premium vehicles before

00:03:21.460 --> 00:03:26.840
local production. The center is the first dedicated location of its kind in the country.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:32.900
While Tesla pushes into new markets, its robot program continues to share incremental progress

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:38.640
updates. Tesla's humanoid robot shared new footage of its latest movements and tasks.

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:44.780
The clip continues the steady drip of progress updates that keep the optimist timeline in public view.

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:49.540
Viewers are watching for signs of improved austerity and real-world utility.

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:55.640
The video shows refined walking and basic object handling. Keep an eye on further FSD

00:03:55.640 --> 00:04:00.880
updates and optimist testing footage in the coming days. That's your Tesla news for today.

